Z||000000||MrPBody||04-29-2001||09:39 AM||||2nd try -- I think the dog ate my first post.<P>A few photos from the Third Annual Fiero Swap Meet:<P><BR>Lots of nice Fieros:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/swap3_002b.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/swap3_003b.jpg"> <P><BR>Indys:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/swap3_004b.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/swap3_011b.jpg"> <P>Rebodies:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/swap3_001b.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/swap3_012b.jpg"> <P><BR>And a few things difficult to recognize as Fieros:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/swap3_015b.jpg"> <P><BR>Oh, yeah -- some parts for sale, too!<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000001||bHooper||04-29-2001||10:16 AM||||ooo, ooo, ooo.... i like the orange formula, and the lue one too... and the white indy's are so pretty, as is the red whateveritis, and the buck rogers space scooter is really neat!  is that really a fiero?!  who brought that one?<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000002||MrPBody||04-29-2001||11:33 AM||||The rear of "Wild Thing" is a Fiero.  The front is . . . I don't know.  Probably motorcycle steering.  For sale with matching trailer.  I don't remember price.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||04-29-2001||07:32 PM||||Got back home from the meet a few hours ago. Had a great time, anytime I'm south of Ohio is great though. I haven't heard the official count, but I think there were just a few more people than last year. Cruised along the tents, checked out what was available. I don't think there was as much busines this year, but I didn't see as many interesting items for sale this year(only 1 item caight my eye, but didn't buy anything). I saw Rodney able to take a break(last year his tent was swamped with people all day), and even Ed was able to walk around without the huge crowds following him like last year. Still, stuff was sold and people bought things. Lots of Fieros out in the lot, more than last year, but fewer trucks. My Formula was out among the parking lots, among the seemingly dozens of other Formulas. Raydar's t-top Formula is a steal, especially compared to the asking prices for a few Fieros there.<BR>Had great time with Boilermaker, WTIII, 87ECO5 and ChadMan. Caravaned back North with them.<P>I think that might be me sitting in the chair on the left of the first picture(my monitor is a POS LCD notebook monitor). I hung out there a bit, was too hot wearing jeans. Had a great trip, wish I was South right now, Ohio sucks.||||reg||7
Z||000004||85Josh||04-29-2001||08:07 PM||||I just rolled in, myself. Sunday was definitely deal day! Got a console for $10, a console support bracket for another ten, and this huge pile of 4-cylinder stuff for ten bucks! If any one needs a 4-cyl coil, e-mail me, I now have two good 84 coils, and two spare 85 coils. Some more stuff too, not sure what all I got. Meet many people, talked up a storm, and got a great sunburn!<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)||||reg||14
Z||000005||Tom88gt||04-29-2001||09:55 PM||||Hey,  Big thanks to "Joey"? in the blue GT from Slidell LA/Gold Coast Fiero.  My Formula's coil ****  on me at the motel.  He was a great help finding the problem and getting parts.  Didn't get a chance to really thank you.  You missed the Joy Luck diner, I was going to pick up the tab.  I owe you one!!!   ||||reg||10
Z||000006||Ronnie||04-29-2001||10:49 PM||||Hey Chuck, glad I got to see you , but then it seems we never crossed paths again. Sorry I didn't get to talk with you more. We had a great time, met a few forum members also. If I talked with anyone and didn't remember who you was , it's because I don't look at the name tags like I should.We did go to the Joy Luck buffet Sat. night with Raydar. Sure would be nice if we could put together more swap meets like that , more often. If anyone knows of any more , let us all know.<BR>Oh yeah, we drove the BLACK 86GT down for this one.<P>------------------<BR>'86GT/'88FORMULA/'88GT<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ronnies_1.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000007||Old Lar||04-29-2001||11:05 PM||||May 5 in Paxton, Illinois at Twin Lakes Autobody is another get together.||||reg||1
Z||000008||85Josh||04-29-2001||11:44 PM||||Hey, I just realized that I'm in the picture! I'm the guy in the cowboy hat, taking a picture of the Wild Thing! Cool. ||||reg||6
Z||000009||Carrolles||04-30-2001||10:32 AM||||I got there about 9:30 Saturday morning and had a great time.  I met a few Forum folks and got some really good deals.  I'm glad I took my van because I loaded it up with goodies.<P>See you there next year.<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000010||Raydar||04-30-2001||04:50 PM||||It was great to see everybody again, and to put faces with the names I see here every day. (Even missed meeting a few folks that I know were there.) <BR>Managed to only spend about half of the funds I brought with me. Of course I didn't quite find all that I was looking for, either.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>Also managed to eat too much at Joy Luck.<BR>(Had to forego the "Bucket of Frozen Margarita"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> that I drank last year, though.)<P>BTW... Kick Hill Farm usually has a swap meet in late summer/fall. Never been to that one. I hear it's pretty good, though.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||14
Z||000011||spideyfoot||04-30-2001||06:07 PM||||Hey folks had fun there last weekend (longhair w yellow hat) learned lots of neat tricks. And for future ref. a console will fit in a trunk. Thanks foor the goodies 85Josh. So did you get it all in your car? Well I cant wait till next year. spideyfoot||||reg||1
Z||000012||Wolfhound||04-30-2001||06:52 PM||||My time at the Swap Meet was short. Wish I could have met more forum members that I know from here and have never seen. Met Mr. Peabody, Songman, Radar, and 85Josh, Rosie Parks and Rodney, and was impressed with all. Really nice folks!! Spent about $250 for some great deals but had too many irons in the fire.<BR>Great weekend, My friends won Hobby Stock at the Huntsville Speedway (2 out of 4). I bought a Fiero and I made it home alive, Well, Katy's not home yet so this may be temporary cause I bought another one when I went through Montgomery. <BR> I have to say I saw so many nice Fieros, the neat thing was as I approached Toney they became common on the road. I love driving Fieros but they look so good when they are on the road and cared for, something you can't see from the inside.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Coy <p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 05-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||MrPBody||04-30-2001||07:47 PM||||It was a pleasure to see Wolfhound, 007Doug, mrfiero, Rodney, and other long-distance Fiero friends. And it seemed that almost everyone from Atlanta was there: Raydar, Paul, Roger, John, Don, Ashby, <I>et al.</I>  Sorry I had to leave Saturday afternoon.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000014||Ronnie||04-30-2001||09:00 PM||||By the way folks, that scooter was for sale for........<BR>$25,000 bucks!!!!! including trailer of course. Got any takers????||||reg||6
Z||000015||Nashco||04-30-2001||11:39 PM||||I agree, it was a very good time.  This was my first Fiero event, and I was somewhat leary of how it would be compared to my usual VW scene.  I was amazed, it was a much friendlier environment (maybe because there aren't so many smoked out hippies and rust collectors)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  I got a bunch of stuff for my car, and met some new people.  I give props to all!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000016||85Josh||05-01-2001||10:22 PM||||Spideyfoot, I got everything but the radiator, fan and rear fascias in the Fiero! I think different people managed to pick up both fascias, and I belive Rosy Parks got the radiator and fan. I looked like the Beverly Hillbilly Fiero, rolling up the road! Went to the Corvette museum on my way home, with 007Doug, and just had a blast all weekend long!<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)||||reg||14
Z||000017||PAUL88GT||05-02-2001||05:07 PM||||It was a great weekend.  I bought about $600 in parts for my 86se restoration.  There were many bargains this year because there were several more parts vendors than last year. You can buy most parts here cheaper than a junkyard and you don't have to pull the parts yourself.<P>Examples: great fender skin: $10, tan seat and seat back covers: $15.  4 saw blade wheels with tires: $50 <P>I enjoyed meeting the following people from the forum:<P>Raydar, Nashco, MrPbody, mrfiero, 007Doug, 87ec..., Chadman, toomanyfieros and his Dad, and several others.<P>That hybrid fiero/airplane/motorcycle is awesome. Both it and the Lamborghini kit car were built by a local retired NASA engineer.  The guy must live in his garage. I had heard about it from several people who had seen it, but were not sure what it was. It has only been finished about a month.  His custom bumper sticker said "My other Fiero is a Lamborghini"<P>One of the best parts is Sunday morning.  The parts that the vendors leave behind are free. Several useful items were left for the vultures who were willing to stay that long.  Can't wait till next year.<P>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000018||DL10||05-02-2001||05:12 PM||||Can someone tell me anything about the red rebody pictured above. Who the owner is .....how much it's for sale for....      do you have any more pics.....Thanks if you can help||||reg||1
Z||000019||PAUL88GT||05-02-2001||06:10 PM||||DL10:<P>That red rebody is an Aldino kit on an 86gt.  The owner is Ron Musing of Huntsville, Alabama.  I think he wants around $25k. I would buy it myself if I thought my marriage could handle it. It is in excellent condition.  He hardly ever drives it.  E-mail me and I will send you his work phone number.  He is not on the forum.<P>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000020||Frank Martin||05-03-2001||10:32 PM||||It was going for $25,000 with trailer and molds.  The problem is that is was not big enough for a person like me<BR> <A HREF="http://spacecoastfieros.com" TARGET=_blank>http://spacecoastfieros.com</A> <P>couple of pictures at the above site<P>Later<P>Frank Martin<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MrPBody:<BR><B>The rear of "Wild Thing" is a Fiero.  The front is . . . I don't know.  Probably motorcycle steering.  For sale with matching trailer.  I don't remember price.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
